load @term/seed/code/structure/ring
  find ring

# A polynomial: a finite sum of powers of variables with coefficients in a ring, the basic object of algebra. Setting a
# polynomial to zero defines a variety, the geometric shape of its solutions, the bridge from algebra to geometry. The
# elementary polynomial identities (the squares, the cubes, the Sophie Germain factorization) are machine-checked in the
# polynomial identity file, and the norm of each rung of the number tower is a polynomial identity. The form carries the
# coefficient ring and an opaque expression; the identities are the theorems.
form polynomial
  link ring, like ring
  link expression, note private
